<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank passes on Kolbenschmidt stake.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank passes on Kolbenschmidt stake.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Commerzbank AG said on Tuesday it had transferred a 24.99 percent stake in car components group Kolbenschmidt AG to a third party.</p>
<p>A bank spokesman said the move was agreed with British engineering group T&amp;N Plc, which has an option to buy Commerzbank's 49.99 percent holding in Kolbenschmidt but has been blocked from doing so by German cartel authorities.</p>
<p>The spokesman declined to say who the third party was and whether T&amp;N still had an option to buy the package.</p>
<p>In the past, the bank has said it did not plan to renew T&amp;N's option, which expires at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
